          "Engage the renter minority (22.8%) with specific housing policy substance even though homeowners dominate: in a district this affluent, renters are often younger professionals or service workers whose housing access and affordability concerns exist alongside the homeowner majority's tax and education priorities; both constituencies deserve material policy engagement.",
          "Maintain consistent substantive messaging on education, healthcare, and tax fairness across all forums: in a 70% college-educated district, voters have the knowledge and information access to detect inconsistency or evasion quickly; clarity and consistency on core policy commitments are the foundation of durable support."
