          { name: "Allowing Housing, Wage, and Healthcare Concerns to Remain Unaddressed or Abstracted", tag: "avoid", why: "In a renter-majority district with a 35.3-year median age and $80,211 income, housing affordability, wage stagnation, and healthcare access are not peripheral policy concerns—they are the material daily reality for nearly half the district and the immediate economic pressures on younger households establishing families. An incumbent who does not offer specific, concrete legislative responses to these issues creates space for a challenger to mobilize by offering them. The unopposed result should not create the false impression that these concerns are adequately addressed or politically resolved; they are likely the primary pressure points in the district and the most effective terrain for any future opposition campaign." }
