          "Lead with concrete delivery on housing affordability and renter-specific economic security: at 53.4% renter majority with $67,785 median income, tenant protection, affordable housing development, and the material cost of rent are not peripheral issues but central to whether younger renters feel the incumbent is delivering for them.",
          "Build durable relationships with the Hispanic community at 15.2%: this is large enough that shifts in turnout or candidate preference materially affect the margin; specific engagement on immigration policy, workplace protections, and economic mobility for Latino households is both constituent obligation and electoral necessity.",
          "Engage college-educated voters on institutional credibility and issue specificity: at 44.5% college-educated, this constituency evaluates on whether the incumbent demonstrates command of policy detail and institutional fluency on education funding, student debt, and healthcare access — not on generic Democratic messaging."
