          "Make education and workforce access a visible legislative priority: the 15.6% college attainment rate in a young district (median age 31.9) is a structural barrier to economic mobility, and a representative who treats higher education funding, community college affordability, and apprenticeship access as core agenda items demonstrates understanding of the district's actual constraints.",
          "Treat the unopposed status as a vulnerability, not a victory: without a challenger in 2024, the incumbent has built no track record of demonstrated constituent benefit; the next cycle will be genuinely competitive unless voters can point to visible economic improvement — housing affordability progress, job creation, or wage increases — that they attribute directly to the representative's legislative work."
