          { name: "Treating Renters as a Marginal Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "The 21.5% renter rate in an affluent suburban district is not marginal—it represents young professionals, empty-nesters, and mobile-income households whose fiscal priorities (housing costs, transportation, service quality) differ meaningfully from homeowners' concerns (property tax, school funding tied to property wealth). A campaign that speaks exclusively to homeowner priorities will forfeit the renter vote to an opponent who addresses their distinct economic concerns. In a 52-48 district, the renter constituency is arithmetically sufficient to determine the outcome, and treating them as peripheral rather than as a distinct voter group with actionable concerns is a strategic error." }
