          "Engage Hispanic residents and younger households directly on economic opportunity, affordable housing policy, and educational access; the 5.81% Hispanic population is the growth vector in this district, and being first to build authentic relationships with this constituency creates a structural advantage.",
          "Monitor demographic shifts closely: the combination of 21.2% renter rate, 5.81% Hispanic population, and 42.0 median age in a $91,393-income district suggests professional migration and family in-movement are reshaping the electorate faster than traditional partisan models account for — treat this as an early-warning signal.",
          "Avoid any messaging that positions education funding, housing affordability, or immigrant economic integration as secondary or threatening to the incumbent coalition; these are not minority issues in a district where they are reshaping who votes, but the political opportunity to define them first belongs to whoever engages them first."
