          "Build specific constituent relationships with the 29.9% renter population and younger adults (median age 32.4): this segment evaluates on housing affordability, school quality, and whether state policy is supporting their economic mobility — not on inherited partisan loyalty. Proactive engagement on affordable housing, education funding, and young-professional workforce development prevents future opposition from winning this constituency by default.",
          "Demonstrate measurable investment in K-12 education funding and school quality improvement: at $95,026 median income with 33.9% college education, suburban voters in HD-43 will evaluate incumbent performance directly on whether schools are well-resourced, teacher compensation is competitive, and their children's educational outcomes are strong — this is not an abstract ideological issue but a material quality-of-life concern that drives voting behavior.",
