          "Lead with housing affordability and economic mobility for young professionals: at 54.4% renters earning $61,265, this constituency is acutely aware that education does not guarantee economic security, and state policy on housing costs, student debt, and workplace rights directly affects whether they remain in Kansas or pursue opportunity elsewhere.",
          "Build authentic relationships with the immigrant professional community represented in the ~7.6% demographic gap: tech workers, healthcare professionals, educators, and business professionals from Asian and other immigrant backgrounds are economically valuable to the district and require specific engagement around credential recognition, workplace discrimination protections, and whether Kansas positions itself as welcoming to immigrant talent.",
          "Develop concrete answers to healthcare access outside employer coverage: for a young, educated, renter-majority constituency, healthcare security is tied to employment stability rather than family networks or retiree Medicare, making Medicaid expansion, marketplace stability, and rural clinic access the material governance issues that distinguish a responsive representative from one coasting on an unopposed mandate."
