          { name: "Assuming a 68% Margin Is Durable Without Demonstrating Governance Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "A 68-32 result in a district of affluent, educated homeowners is not a mandate for passivity — it is a margin earned through demonstrated competence and held only if that competence is continuously demonstrated. Affluent homeowners have choices and make voting decisions based on whether they believe their representative is competently stewardship their interests. Any incumbent or challenger who campaigns this seat as though 68% represents an uncontestable base and does not actively engage on the specific fiscal, infrastructure, and development issues that matter to this constituency will find the margin eroded by a credible alternative." },
          { name: "Allowing National Partisan Messaging to Crowd Out Local Governance Issues", tag: "avoid", why: "KS-HD-54's 31% college attainment and $84,017 median income describe a constituency of professionals and business people who evaluate representatives on local competence and local issues, not on national partisan positioning. A representative who relies on national Republican messaging instead of demonstrating specific understanding of the district's property tax, school funding, infrastructure, and development policy challenges will lose the persuasion of college-educated swing voters who have the resources and information to evaluate alternatives. Local governance competence is the currency of this district; national talking points are not." }
