          "Engage college-educated adults (34.2%) as policy evaluators, not partisan targets: this constituency demands substance on education funding, healthcare access, and environmental or economic policy specifics; candidates who lead with personality or partisan rhetoric without substantive policy grounding will lose credibility with the 34.2% of the district that votes on policy rather than identity.",
          "Build active renter constituency engagement: at 40.8%, renters represent two-fifths of HD-56 households with direct economic stakes in housing markets, landlord regulation, and tenant protections; any candidate who treats homeowner interests as the default constituent focus will systematically underperform among the renter majority.",
          "Address Hispanic community (10.73%) with specific economic and immigration-policy engagement: Hispanic voters in this income range are evaluating on whether state policy supports economic mobility, workplace fairness, and immigration enforcement proportionality; treating this constituency as a bloc vote without differentiated outreach misses persuadable voters who may weigh multiple policy dimensions."
