          { name: "Assuming Hispanic Voters Will Respond to Abstract Democratic Positioning", tag: "avoid", why: "Hispanic voters in Kansas are pragmatic evaluators of candidates on direct constituent service, economic opportunity, and whether government is delivering for their households — not reflexive partisan voters. Any campaign strategy that treats the 25.28% Hispanic constituency as a locked voting bloc to be activated with generic Democratic messaging about rights or identity politics without specific answers to healthcare access, education quality, and economic mobility will lose 3-5 points of Hispanic support relative to 2024. This constituency requires direct, material-focused engagement on their actual governance concerns, not abstract partisan framing." }
