          "Investigate and address the 4.74% demographic gap with specificity—whether American Indian, additional Hispanic, or other communities, these 2,000-3,000 residents are invisible in the data but real in the district. Constituent attention to their economic and civic concerns, rather than assumption of inherited Republican loyalty, builds durable support and reduces vulnerability to challenger mobilization.",
          "Lead with middle-income economic security and workforce opportunity: at $70,663 income with 25.7% college attainment, this is a constituency whose children's economic mobility depends on state workforce development, affordable higher education access, and real job creation in Kansas. This is the material issue most likely to resonate across the homeowner majority and younger adult minority simultaneously.",
          "Engage the renter constituency directly on housing affordability and economic mobility—27.4% renter rate in a Republican district this strong suggests these voters are not reliably voting their economic interests. Specific policy attention to rental market regulation, housing supply, and wage stagnation relative to cost of living is the messaging most likely to consolidate support and discourage competitive challenges."
