          { name: "Defaulting to Culture-War Positioning in a Professional-Class District", tag: "avoid", why: "A constituency with 59.5% college attainment, $83,620 income, and 35.0 median age — the educated professional-class core of Kansas politics — evaluates on material economic concerns before cultural positioning. A candidate who leads with cultural conservatism rather than housing affordability, wage growth, and economic opportunity is misdiagnosing the persuasion vectors in a district where college-educated professionals, renters, and younger adults have real economic security concerns that transcend partisan identity. This is especially true in a 52-48 seat where the opposition is persuadable, not ideologically fixed." }
