          "Lead with young renter economic security: housing cost burden, healthcare access, and wage growth are the material concerns of a 27.3-year-old, 53.6%-renting constituency at $55,969 income; any successor who addresses these concerns with specificity rather than inherited Republican framing will hold Butler's margin more durably than one who assumes it transfers automatically.",
          "Engage Hispanic and Black communities with targeted constituent attention: at 13.63% and 12.87% respectively, these are significant constituencies whose economic mobility concerns in a renting, working-class district are directly actionable through state policy on housing, wages, and healthcare access.",
