          "Engage the Hispanic community with specific constituent attention: at 9.61% of the district and concentrated in renters and working-class households, the Hispanic community's concerns about housing affordability, wage protection, and healthcare access are real and present, and require direct engagement rather than generic minority outreach.",
          "Build legislative record on working-class economic security, not partisan positioning: a 41.8-year-old, 35.3% renter, $61,696-income constituency evaluates on whether government is solving their material problems, not on ideological messaging — any campaign that leads with partisan framing rather than concrete problem-solving will underperform the district's underlying political vulnerability."
