          "Engage the Hispanic (5.89%) and Black (2.03%) populations with visible constituent attention and economic integration into the professional economy; at less than 8% of the district they are currently too small to swing the seat, but their growth trajectory and the professional majority's openness to swing voting make early authentic engagement a smart preventive investment.",
          "Do not treat 100% unopposed as a durable majority position; the demographic profile of college-educated professionals and higher-income homeowners is precisely the swing constituency that national and Kansas politics have shown can be mobilized by a credible challenger offering superior governance on education, healthcare, or tax policy.",
          "Monitor whether the professional majority perceives the incumbent as delivering on K-12 education quality, healthcare affordability, and local economic opportunity — the three governance issues most salient to this income and education demographic — and respond aggressively if dissatisfaction emerges."
