          { name: "Ignoring the ~15% AIAN/AIAN Demographic Gap as Electorally Irrelevant", tag: "avoid", why: "The ~15.27% of the district's population not captured in the four reported Census categories represents tribal governments and Native American constituents whose relationship to state policy exists independent of whether they voted in the last election. Treating this constituency as electorally irrelevant because they do not appear in the partisan margin is a governance failure—it means serving 85% of the district while ignoring the material needs of the remaining 15%. This is both a governing obligation and a potential electoral vulnerability if the tribal community organizes alternative representation." }
