          "Monitor the district's economic trajectory carefully; as rural Kansas consolidates and younger adults migrate to larger towns for opportunity, districts with 42.3-year median age can age rapidly, creating a constituency increasingly dependent on fixed incomes and increasingly vulnerable to economic frustration if the representative is not delivering tangible results."
