          { name: "Defaulting to Abstract Conservative Messaging in a Material Economic Anxiety District", tag: "avoid", why: "A district where nearly one-third are renters, median income is $54K, and college attainment is 20.5% is not a natural home for ideological messaging about government size or abstract principle. These households are evaluating on whether their rent is affordable, whether their wages are rising, whether they can access healthcare, and whether their kids have a pathway to better outcomes. Candidates who lead with economic anxiety are more credible here than candidates who lead with conservative principle divorced from material household pressures." }
