          { name: "Ignoring the Renter Majority or Positioning Renters as Opposed to Homeowner Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "At 48%, renters are not a minority constituency or a special interest — they are the district's largest single housing group and represent households with material economic concerns around housing cost and mobility. Any candidate whose messaging or legislative record positions renter interests as opposed to homeowner prosperity will find that framing alienates the largest single constituency in the district and creates an opening for the opposition to consolidate renter support. In a 51-49 seat, the capacity to hold renters as persuadable rather than allowing them to consolidate against the incumbent is the difference between winning and losing." }
