          "Maintain active constituent service and legislative track record visibility: a 66-34 margin is not permission to reduce engagement; it is a baseline that requires continuous demonstration that the incumbent is delivering on local priorities and remaining responsive to the specific concerns of an educated, affluent constituency that evaluates on performance.",
          "Address the renter minority with specific attention: at only 18.9% renters, this population can become invisible in a district this homeowner-dominant, but they are present enough to matter in a tight race, and their housing affordability and quality-of-life concerns are real — ignoring them creates an opening for opposition organizing.",
          "Avoid taking the 66-34 result as permission to reduce legislative effort or constituent attention: this is a consolidated constituency, not a growing one, and the margin depends on continued perceived competence in addressing the specific governance concerns of affluent, educated homeowners — complacency is the primary risk to holding the seat."
