          { name: "Ignoring the Renter Majority's Distinct Economic Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "With 47.1% renters, a representative who organizes around homeowner priorities — property tax relief, building permit streamlining, land development — is serving only 53% of the constituency. Renters' primary concerns are rental affordability, landlord accountability, and the cost of living in their current housing situation. Any legislator whose platform is implicitly homeowner-focused is leaving the renter majority without representation and creating an opening for a challenger who speaks directly to their material needs." }
