          "Engage the ~3.91% AIAN gap population with specific constituent attention: while smaller than in other districts, American Indian or Alaska Native residents still represent several hundred voters who deserve acknowledgment and engagement rather than assumption into the broader working-class narrative.",
          "Do not assume the 59% result creates a safe seat: in a district where nearly half are renters at below-median income, economic vulnerability is high and voter satisfaction is conditional on material delivery; any incumbent who campaigns on the margin rather than on concrete improvements in constituent living standards risks credible competition in the next cycle."
