          { name: "Ignoring Economic Stress Among the 21% Renter Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where 79% of households own their homes, the 21% renter population is economically distinct and politically invisible if the incumbent's entire messaging and advocacy focuses on homeowner concerns. Younger working adults and renters in rural Kansas face real constraints on housing affordability, wage growth, and economic mobility; an incumbent who treats these constituents as peripheral to the district's core political identity neglects 21% of the population and forfeits the opportunity to build durable support among the demographic cohort most likely to remain in the district long-term." }
