          "Lead with older homeowner economic security: property tax fairness, healthcare cost management, and the viability of rural infrastructure and services in a community with declining population density and rising fixed costs are the concrete concerns that determine whether an 80% margin holds.",
          "Engage the 21% renter constituency and younger working adults on housing affordability and wage growth—they are the economic-mobility constituency in a district where 79% homeownership masks real constraint on entry-level households, and neglecting their concerns creates vulnerability to any challenger who addresses affordability.",
          "Maintain consistent, responsive constituent service and local accountability; an 80% incumbent margin depends on the perception that the representative is delivering on material local concerns, not on partisan loyalty alone. Any perception of inattention to property taxes, healthcare access, or rural service decline will erode the margin in a primary challenge or general election."
