          "Lead with constituent service and district-specific governance — not abstract partisan messaging — as the mechanism to consolidate the supermajority: younger, college-educated voters in competitive states evaluate representatives on whether they deliver concrete results on healthcare access, education funding, and cost-of-living pressure, not on inherited Republican loyalty.",
          "Build relationships with the renter community and younger professionals in HD-111 through targeted constituent attention on housing affordability, student debt, and workplace healthcare access; the 40.3% renter rate and 31.4-year median age represent a constituency that can vote against a well-positioned incumbent if they perceive their economic concerns are being ignored.",
          "Do not assume the 73% result indicates a durable base: in neighboring competitive Kansas and Colorado districts, 70%+ Republican margins have collapsed when Democratic candidates targeted college-educated and younger voters with specific economic messaging. Proactive engagement with the college-educated and renter constituencies is the mechanism to prevent HD-111 from becoming a target in a future cycle."
