          "Lead with middle-income economic security: at $74,726 median income with 22.5% renters, this is a constituency managing housing costs, healthcare inflation, and wage stagnation; property tax fairness, healthcare affordability, and job-quality issues are the material governance concerns that will determine durability against a future challenger.",
          "Build constituent-service infrastructure that is visible and accessible to both the Anglo majority and the Hispanic minority; unopposed seats often become complacent, but this one has nearly one-quarter of its population in a demographic category that could become a mobilized opposition constituency if underserved.",
          "Avoid treating the unopposed context as evidence of deep constituent satisfaction or electoral safety; instead, use it as an opportunity to establish proactive engagement with minority communities, renters, younger adults, and other constituencies that may not have been prioritized in previous cycles."
