          "Avoid treating 81% as evidence of invulnerability — while the Democratic electoral threat is negligible, internal Republican dynamics or genuine constituent dissatisfaction around rural economic concerns are the only plausible challenge vectors in this district; an incumbent who becomes complacent about constituent service or rural economic issues risks allowing a primary challenger to establish that the incumbent has taken the seat for granted."
