          { name: "Treating the District as Demographically Homogeneous", tag: "avoid", why: "The 89.17% white demographic, while substantial, obscures the ~3.92% unaccounted-for population and should not be used as justification for ignoring minority constituencies or assuming their passive support. In a district this close to the Midwest, any rural or small-town Kansas constituency will have Native American residents, and potentially immigrant or refugee populations connected to agricultural employment, whose needs and civic participation are real and present. A representative who builds only the Anglo homeowner coalition and assumes everyone else will simply remain politically inactive is vulnerable to a challenger who takes those communities seriously." }
