          { name: "Dismissing the Renter Constituency as Electorally Insignificant", tag: "avoid", why: "At 28.4% of the district, renters represent nearly one-third of the population and in an affluent professional district are likely younger professionals, service-sector workers, and families in transition—constituents with real interests in housing affordability, rental market regulation, and tenant protections that are often invisible in homeowner-focused campaigns. Dismissing this constituency or treating their concerns as secondary means ceding a meaningful slice of the electorate to a challenger willing to address their specific material interests; in a 66-34 district, losing a portion of the renter vote to a focused opposition campaign could narrow the margin significantly." }
