          "Engage the 28.4% renter constituency directly: renters in high-income districts are often younger professionals, service-sector workers, or families in transition; housing affordability, rental market regulation, and tenant protections are material issues for this subset that can become invisible in homeowner-focused campaigns.",
          "Treat the 34% opposition as a credible swing constituency, not a base to ignore: a challenger who runs a competent, issue-focused campaign in a district this affluent and educated can expand that 34% meaningfully; the incumbent cannot assume the margin is stable without active constituent engagement on governance performance and priority alignment."
