          "Address young adult economic concerns directly: with median age 29.8 and 26.2% college attainment in a working-class district, this constituency evaluates on wage trajectory, job quality, and whether government is reducing or increasing financial barriers to stability — abstract conservative positioning will not hold this cohort if a challenger offers concrete economic alternatives.",
          "Treat the 40% opposition as evidence of real constituent concerns, not as a base to dismiss: understand specifically whether it concentrates among renters frustrated by housing costs, among young adults skeptical of government support for economic mobility, or among Latino voters perceiving insufficient community engagement — and address each with policy substance rather than partisan rhetoric."
