          { name: "Over-Reliance on Party Discipline Without Constituent Attention", tag: "avoid", why: "In a solidly Republican district, the temptation is to default to party-line voting and messaging without demonstrating specific constituent responsiveness. This is a strategic error: the 36% Democratic opposition and the relatively modest college-attainment rate (32.8%) mean many voters evaluate on demonstrated local results — school quality, tax fairness, constituent service — rather than statewide party positioning. A candidate who votes conservatively but demonstrates negligible constituent attention is vulnerable to a Republican challenger who combines conservative votes with visible constituent service." }
