          "Engage the ~5.8% demographic gap thoughtfully — whether those residents are Native American, immigrant, or other non-white constituents — with concrete constituent service and policy recognition; a margin this large can accommodate genuine pluralism without threatening the Republican base, and dismissing nearly 6% of the population as irrelevant is both poor governance and unnecessary electoral risk.",
          "Monitor the 27% opposition for composition and motivation — whether concentrated among renters, younger adults, or specific issue constituencies — and ensure that legislative record actively speaks to their material concerns (housing affordability, economic opportunity, healthcare access) rather than assuming they are unreachable; a 73% result can narrow quickly if opposition mobilizes around specific grievances the incumbent has ignored.",
          "Maintain active presence in local civic, agricultural, and faith institutions where the homeowner base organizes itself; a 73% result is durable when the legislator is genuinely embedded in the community's governing relationships, not simply favored at election time."
