          { name: "Partisan Ideology Over Specific Rural Governance", tag: "avoid", why: "Rural Kansas voters evaluate on whether government delivers concrete results—water security, healthcare access, tax fairness—not on partisan positioning or cultural messaging divorced from material impact. A legislator who campaigns on abstract conservative principles without specific answers to agricultural water policy, rural hospital funding, or rural broadband infrastructure will find the 71% margin vulnerable to a challenger who does offer specifics. This constituency cares what the government does, not what the government says." }
