          "Lead on aging homeowner economic security: property tax fairness, Medicare sustainability, rural hospital access, and infrastructure investment are the concrete policy issues that matter to a 43.8-year-old, 76% homeowner constituency at $59,588 income; these are not ideological positions but direct economic concerns.",
          "Build active constituent services infrastructure—casework responsiveness, town halls focused on healthcare access and economic concerns, and visible presence in rural communities—because the next challenger will emerge by demonstrating that the incumbent has become distant or inattentive.",
          "Do not campaign this seat as safe; the 100% result is organizational absence, not voter satisfaction, and any incumbent who consolidates only the existing Republican base without addressing the economic concerns of older, fixed-income households creates space for a more engaged challenger."
